cff-version: "1.2.0"
title: "simd-ml-kernels: hand-vectorized SIMD kernels for machine learning workloads"
authors:
  - family-names: "Myet"
    given-names: "Min Htet"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-06-09"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mattral/simd-ml-kernels"
url: "https://zenodo.org/records/20616502"
abstract: >
  An open-source C++17 library of clean, well-documented hand-vectorized
  microkernels for GEMM and ML activation functions (GeLU, ReLU, SiLU,
  Softmax, LayerNorm) targeting x86 processors with AVX2/FMA support.
  Includes Python/NumPy bindings via pybind11, a statistical benchmark
  harness, and a CI pipeline with performance regression gating.
keywords:
  - simd
  - avx2
  - avx-512
  - gemm
  - machine-learning
  - microkernels
  - gelu
  - layer-normalization
  - high-performance-computing
  - cpp
